    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-17 (round 18, htrac-frontend deep dive).**\n\n**Symptom.** The javascript-v1 analyzer emits zero import edges from any first-party TypeScript/JavaScript file in hypergumbo's codebase, despite those files having 15+ actual `import ... from \"...\"` statements. Comparable Python files have 4-10x as many import edges as the source code has import statements (due to expansion of `from X import a, b, c` style).\n\n**Reproduction.**\n\n```bash\nhypergumbo run --out /tmp/r18.json --no-sketch-fan-out --no-handler-slices .\n\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nfrom collections import Counter\nd = json.load(open('/tmp/r18.json'))\nnodes_by_id = {n['id']: n for n in d['nodes']}\nimport_ets = {'ast_import', 'import_static', 'import_resolution', 'import_to_manifest', 'npm_package_import'}\nby_path = Counter()\nfor e in d['edges']:\n    et = (e.get('meta') or {}).get('evidence_type')\n    if et in import_ets:\n        src = nodes_by_id.get(e.get('src'), {})\n        if src.get('language') in ('typescript', 'javascript') and 'node_modules' not in (src.get('path') or ''):\n            by_path[src.get('path')] += 1\nfor p, c in sorted(by_path.items()):\n    print(f'  {p}: {c}')\n\"\n```\n\n**Output (May 17):**\n\n```\n<external>: 27\npackages/htrac-frontend/public/service-worker.js: 0\npackages/htrac-frontend/src/components/item-detail.ts: 0\npackages/htrac-frontend/src/components/item-list.ts: 0\npackages/htrac-frontend/src/components/tracker-app.ts: 0\npackages/htrac-frontend/src/main.ts: 0\npackages/htrac-frontend/src/sw-register.ts: 0\npackages/htrac-frontend/src/ws-client.ts: 0\npackages/htrac-frontend/vite.config.ts: 0\n```\n\nAll 8 first-party TS/JS files: 0 import edges each. The 27 edges from `<external>` are synthesized by js-module-linker-v1 (external_symbol → package, not real-file → real-file imports).\n\n**Per-file ground truth vs captured (TS):**\n\n| file | actual imports | captured import edges |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| main.ts | 3 | 0 |\n| tracker-app.ts | 5 | 0 |\n| item-list.ts | 3 | 0 |\n| item-detail.ts | 3 | 0 |\n| vite.config.ts | 1 | 0 |\n| ws-client.ts | 0 | 0 |\n| sw-register.ts | 0 | 0 |\n\n**Per-file ground truth vs captured (Python comparison):**\n\n| file | actual imports | captured | breakdown |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| tracker/cli.py | 12 | 60 | ast_import: 60 |\n| tracker/serve.py | 6 | 24 | ast_import: 21, import_to_manifest: 3 |\n| core/cli.py | 88 | 198 | ast_import: 197, import_to_manifest: 1 |\n\nPython over-captures (expansion of multi-import statements). TS under-captures: literally zero.\n\n**The analyzer DOES know about the imports.** It correctly resolves cross-file calls via the imports:\n\n```\nmain.ts (module) -> ast_call_direct -> connectWebSocket @ ws-client.ts\nmain.ts (module) -> ast_call_direct -> registerServiceWorker @ sw-register.ts\n```\n\nSo the parse + symbol-resolution path works for calls. The gap is specifically in **emitting an ast_import (or equivalent) evidence_type edge for each import statement** so that downstream graph queries like \"what does this file import?\" can answer.\n\n**Why this matters.**\n\n- Slice / reverse-slice traversal that follows imports cannot start from a TS file's import statements.\n- Dependency-mapping tools that ask \"which files import X?\" miss all TS callers.\n- Module-level provenance is incomplete (the call-graph edges go function-to-function, skipping the file-import layer).\n- INV-popop (route stable_id collisions) and adjacent linker work depends on accurate import edges for cross-file resolution.\n\n**Root cause hypothesis.** `packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/src/hypergumbo_lang_mainstream/js_ts.py` is where the JS/TS extraction lives. Either:\n\n1. The analyzer parses import statements but doesn't construct Edge objects for them, OR\n2. The Edge objects are constructed but use a meta.evidence_type that isn't in the set hypergumbo recognizes as \"import\" (and is therefore invisible to the test above), OR\n3. The Edges target the wrong src node (e.g., the file-kind node rather than the module-kind node, or vice-versa).\n\nQuick check on (2): I scanned all evidence_types from TS source nodes — no obvious \"import-shaped\" name beyond `ast_import`, `import_static`, `import_resolution`. So this is most likely (1) — the JS/TS analyzer just doesn't emit import edges.\n\n**Fix.** When the JS/TS analyzer parses an `import` statement, emit an Edge with:\n- `src`: the module-kind node for the importing file\n- `dst`: the module-kind node for the imported file (or external_symbol if cross-package)\n- `meta.evidence_type`: `ast_import` (to match Python's convention) or a TS-specific equivalent that test utilities recognize\n\nAdd a regression test: a 2-file TS repo where file_a imports from file_b produces at least one ast_import edge with src=file_a's module and dst=file_b's module.\n\n**Severity.** High — this is a structural import-edge production gap affecting ALL TypeScript/JavaScript first-party code analyzed by hypergumbo. Currently only Python imports surface in the graph.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- INV-ronuf (websocket linker phantom file Symbols) — adjacent (TS file representation), filed earlier.\n- INV-hojus (Python files double-represented as kind=file + kind=module) — adjacent (file-vs-module identity), filed earlier.\n- WI-vurop (JS/TS unresolved-call edges for namespace imports) — CALLS work; IMPORTS don't.\n- WI-pinop, WI-kujom — adjacent JS/TS call-resolution work.\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 18 section."  # 6018
    fields:  # 6018
      statement: "The javascript-v1 analyzer must emit an Edge for every import statement in TS/JS source files. Currently 0 import edges are emitted from any first-party TS/JS file in hypergumbo's codebase, despite ground-truth count of 15+ import statements across 7 first-party TS files. Python analyzer correctly emits ast_import edges (8.8/file avg). The JS/TS analyzer DOES parse imports internally (cross-file ast_call_direct edges resolve correctly) but does not emit an ast_import evidence_type Edge for each import statement."  # 6018
      root_cause: "Hypothesized: js_ts.py constructs cross-file call edges using internal import resolution but never wraps the import statements themselves as Edge objects with meta.evidence_type='ast_import' (or any other import-related evidence_type). Fix: in js_ts.py's import-parsing path, emit Edge(src=importing module-node, dst=imported module-node or external_symbol, meta.evidence_type='ast_import'). Regression test: 2-file TS repo where file_a has 'import { x } from \"./file_b.js\"' produces ast_import edge from file_a's module to file_b's module."  # 6018
