  message: "REFINEMENT (2026-05-17 deeper dig): Original claim 'zero import edges' was based on querying meta.evidence_type. Using top-level edge.type='imports' instead reveals 27 TS imports DO exist — but ALL 27 have src=<external_symbol> pseudo-node, not the module-kind Symbol of the importing source file.\n\nSo the actual gap is more specific: the JS/TS analyzer DOES emit edge_type='imports' edges, but with src wired to an external_symbol stand-in (e.g., 'external_symbol: main.ts') rather than to the real module-kind Symbol ('typescript:packages/.../main.ts:1-27:<module:main.ts>:module'). Same dst-side too — both endpoints are external_symbol pseudo-nodes.\n\nDownstream impact unchanged: a graph query 'what does typescript:.../main.ts:<module> import?' still returns 0 results, because no import edges have that module-kind node as src.\n\nProducer split:\n- javascript-v1: 15 edges (import_static evidence)\n- js-module-linker-v1: 12 edges (import_resolution + ast_import evidence)\n\nFix should target wherever js_ts.py decides which node to use as edge.src for import-relationship edges. It's choosing external_symbol when it should be choosing the file's module-kind Symbol (same approach Python uses — Python's 10009 import edges have src=python-module-kind Symbol of the file)."  # bf2c
